{
  "_": [
    "What every surface in the application shell measures, in both themes, recomputed",
    "from src/index.head.html's own token tables by tools/verify_theme.mjs.",
    "",
    "kind: text    -> 4.5:1  (WCAG 1.4.3; everything here is under 18.66px)",
    "      large   -> 3.0:1  (>=24px, or >=18.66px bold)",
    "      graphic -> 3.0:1  (WCAG 1.4.11: an icon, a fill or a state marker)",
    "      state   -> 1.1:1  between two BACKGROUNDS, which is the only way to ask",
    "                        whether a hover or a current-item tint is visible at all.",
    "                        Not a WCAG number: 1.00 is what .inav:hover measured in",
    "                        the light theme, and 1.1 is the floor that catches it.",
    "",
    "A background stack is written outermost-last and composites down onto --ground.",
    "bgLight overrides bg when the light theme re-declares that surface (.rail does).",
    "",
    "A state entry with \"from\" does not restate the hover colour: the gate reads it out",
    "of that rule, and out of its [data-theme=light] twin, falling back to the dark value",
    "when the twin is missing. That fallback IS the .inav:hover defect, so it is measured",
    "rather than described.",
    "",
    "sel  -> the rule the INK comes from. When present the gate reads that rule's `color`",
    "        (or `prop`) out of the stylesheet in both themes and IGNORES `fg`, so putting",
    "        a surface back on the token it used to have moves the measured number and the",
    "        gate fails. Without `sel` an entry only describes the stylesheet: it was that",
    "        way for every entry until cycle 11, which fed 14 reverts of a fixed surface",
    "        through this gate and had 12 of them accepted. `bg` stays declared here",
    "        because a background STACK is a fact about the DOM, not about one rule.",
    "floor-> a surface deliberately held below the standard floor, e.g. a placeholder that",
    "        must stay quieter than the value it stands in for. It is excluded from the",
    "        headline 'tightest text', or adding one would look like a regression."
  ],
